      "answer": "Rule-based reward models (RBRMs) are zero-shot GPT-4 classifiers used to provide an additional reward signal during RLHF fine-tuning, steering GPT-4 towards appropriate behavior [D2]. They were used to reward GPT-4 for refusing harmful requests and for not refusing safe ones, with rubrics defining desired or undesired response styles [D3]. RBRMs help maintain a balance between helpfulness and safety by classifying outputs into categories like safe non-refusal, refusal in desired style, or containing disallowed content [W3]. This technique is part of OpenAI's safety stack, enhancing model safety without relying heavily on recurrent human inputs [W1].",
